{'symbol': 'JNJ', 'date': '2022-08-08 18:45:00', 'title': 'MATHAI MAMMEN, M.D., PH.D., LEAVES POSITION AS EXECUTIVE VICE PRESIDENT, PHARMACEUTICALS, R&D, JOHNSON & JOHNSON', 'text': 'NEW BRUNSWICK, N.J.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--JOHNSON & JOHNSON (NYSE: JNJ) (“THE COMPANY”) ANNOUNCED TODAY THAT MATHAI MAMMEN, M.D., PH.D., HAS DECIDED TO LEAVE HIS POSITION AS EXECUTIVE VICE PRESIDENT, PHARMACEUTICALS, R&D, AND PURSUE OTHER OPPORTUNITIES OUTSIDE OF THE COMPANY. WILLIAM HAIT, M.D., PH.D., WILL SERVE AS INTERIM HEAD OF THE PHARMACEUTICAL R&D ORGANIZATION UNTIL NEW LEADERSHIP IS IDENTIFIED. DR. MAMMEN JOINED JOHNSON & JOHNSON IN 2017 AS GLOBAL HEAD OF JANSSEN R&D, AN'}